---
const mailtoBody = encodeURIComponent(`Product URL:

Flow that breaks:

What users do instead:

What this costs you:

Who needs the review:

Evidence available:
`);
const snapshot = [
  ['Review', 'Hidden Scaffold Review'],
  ['Unit', 'One critical SaaS flow'],
  ['Output', 'failure point · hidden assumption · cost transfer · next scaffold'],
  ['Best fit', 'onboarding · intake · AI-assisted flow · support-heavy moment'],
];
---
<section id="hero" class="console-section hero-console">
  <div class="container console-grid hero-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="hero-label">GUIDANCE FAILURE ARCHITECTURE</div>
      <h1>Your product is losing money where guidance disappears.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subheadline">Your product is not losing users because the interface is ugly. It is losing them where the system asks for action before the next move has been made legible.</p>
      <p class="hero-summary hero-summary-large">I help SaaS and software teams locate the hidden breakdown inside the flow everyone keeps re-explaining: onboarding that delays activation, intake that creates unusable data, AI flows that increase uncertainty, dashboards that inform without directing action, and support-heavy moments the product should have handled earlier.</p>
      <p class="authority-line">Not a UI pass. A read of where the missing scaffold becomes operational cost.</p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href={`mailto:yassergandhi.dev@gmail.com?subject=Hidden%20Scaffold%20Review&body=${mailtoBody}`} class="btn-primary">Send the flow that breaks</a>
        <a href="#offer" class="btn-outline">See what the review includes</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="diagnostic-panel" aria-label="Review Snapshot">
      <div class="panel-kicker">Review Snapshot</div>
      <dl class="snapshot-list">
        {snapshot.map(([label, value]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
